FILE-10: reject nan, inf, hex and empty tokens in getfloat

getfloat() accepted anything strtod() could parse, which includes "nan",
"inf", "infinity" and hexadecimal numbers such as "0x64", and its test
for characters left after the number, *endptr > 0, was false for an
empty token and, where char is signed, for a trailing byte above 127.
NaN then passed every range check, because those are ordered
comparisons. getfloat() now requires the whole token to be read, and
rejects hexadecimal forms and results that are not finite (which also
catches values that overflow, such as 1e999). The locale handling is
unchanged.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-10_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/input2.c b/src/input2.c
index 220c757..8e010e3 100644
--- a/src/input2.c
+++ b/src/input2.c
@@ -718,7 +718,10 @@ int getfloat(char *s, double *y)
         freelocale(locale);
     }    
 
-    if (*endptr > 0) return 0;
+    // Reject an empty token, characters after the number, and the
+    // hexadecimal, infinity and NaN forms that strtod also accepts
+    if (endptr == s || *endptr != '\0') return 0;
+    if (strpbrk(s, "xX") != NULL || !isfinite(*y)) return 0;
     return 1;
 }
 
